{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining mismatch comes from the compiler algebraically collapsing `x * (1 / d)` into `x / d`, skipping the reference’s rounded sigmoid intermediate. I’m forcing that intermediate through the output buffer inside the same Triton launch, then reloading and multiplying. This retains the required FP32 rounding, still removes a launch, and uses less total memory traffic than two separate eager kernels."}}
